## Get Microclimate Data

Here, we will extract microclimate data for the Rothamsted site Broom's Barn for 2024. We will need to set seperate bounding boxes for each site to avoid downloading huge .nc files.

```{r}
#| warning: false
#| echo: false

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Example run at one trap
# The microclimate must be run separately for each species because Usrhyt
# (height in the crop) and shade differ. The minshade/maxshade in micro must
# match the values passed to ectotherm.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#get bbox of our trap sites
roth_coords <- read.csv(here("data", "rothamsted_coordinates.csv"))

bbox <- st_bbox(st_multipoint(matrix(c(roth_coords[,3],roth_coords[,2]),ncol=2)))

years<-seq(1990,2020,by=1)
#buildmcera5 request

reqs <- lapply(years, function(y) {
  build_era5_request(xmin = bbox[["xmin"]], xmax = bbox[["xmax"]],
                     ymin = bbox[["ymin"]], ymax = bbox[["ymax"]],
                     start_time = as.POSIXct(paste0(y, "-01-01 00:00"), tz = "UTC"),
                     end_time   = as.POSIXct(paste0(y, "-12-31 23:00"), tz = "UTC"),
                     outfile_name = paste0("era5_roth_", y))
})
#apply build_era5_request across years in parallel


# Download in parallel; CDS only runs a few requests per user at once
plan(multisession, workers = 4)
future_walk(reqs, function(r) {
  request_era5(request = r, out_path = here("data", "mcera5"), overwrite = FALSE)
}, .options = furrr_options(seed = TRUE, packages = c("mcera5", "here")))
plan(sequential)
```
